"ocr": "\n\nNew Jersey\n\nEagar, Archibald  \nor  \nEdgar\n\nN. 850\n\nCatharine\n\nMP\n\nBOUNTY LAND WARRANT RECORD CARD\\*\n\nNAME Eager, Archibald GRADE Private LINE New Jersey\n\nWARRANT NUMBER 8290 ACREAGE 100 ISSUED September 18, 1799  \nTo Demas Ford\n\n\\*The information concerning the issuance of warrants carded on this form is found in volumes 2 to 4 of \"Land Warrants Issued Prior to 1800\" which are registers of bounty land warrants issued to non-commissioned officers and privates under congressional resolutions of September 16, 1776, and subsequent dates. Other records relative to the applications for warrants appear to have been destroyed in the War Department fire of November 9, 1800. Information concerning warrants surrendered to the Federal Government is to be found in General Land Office records in The National Archives."
